// Getting started with WCL the language. Install + write + check + edit; wdoc is a tail section.
page getting_started { sites = [:wcl]  title = "Getting started"
  h1 "Getting started"

  p "Install the CLI, write a config, validate it, then explore — formatting, the REPL, and the language server, and finally rendering a documentation site with wdoc."

  h2 "1. Install"

  p "Install the `wcl` CLI from a source checkout:"
  code bash {
    source = <<'BASH'
      cargo install --git https://github.com/wiltaylor/wcl -p wcl --locked
    BASH
  }

  h2 "2. Write a config"

  p "Declare a schema with decorators, then author data that matches it. `@inline(0)` binds the block label to a field; `@default` supplies a value when one is omitted; `@children` collects every nested block of a kind."
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
// site.wcl
@block("service")
type Service {
  @inline(0)   name: utf8
  @default(80) port: u32
  region: utf8
}

@document
type Config {
  @children("service") services: list<Service>
}

service "web" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}
service "api" {
  port   = 9090u32
  region = "eu-west-1"
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "3. Check & evaluate"

  p "`wcl check` validates the document against its `@document` schema — exit `0` is OK, `1` a parse error, `2` a schema violation. `wcl eval` (alias `wcl get`) reads any value out by dotted path; `--json` emits a machine-readable form."
  code bash {
    source = <<'BASH'
wcl check site.wcl
wcl eval  site.wcl services
wcl get   site.wcl services --json
BASH
  }

  h2 "4. Format & edit"

  p "`wcl fmt` reformats canonically while preserving comments and blank-line grouping. `wcl set` rewrites a field at a dotted path with a new WCL expression, following imports back to the file that declares it (quote shell-special values)."
  code bash {
    source = <<'BASH'
wcl fmt site.wcl --in-place
wcl set site.wcl service.web.region '"eu-west-2"'
wcl set site.wcl service.api.port 9091u32
BASH
  }

  h2 "5. Editor support"

  p "`wcl lsp` is a full language server (diagnostics, completion, hover, go-to-definition, code actions). It speaks stdio by default."
  callout "VS Code + tree-sitter" {
    class = ["tip"]
    body  = "editors/vscode ships a minimal VS Code extension that spawns wcl lsp; editors/tree-sitter-wcl is a tree-sitter grammar stub for editors that consume them."
  }

  h2 "6. (Optional) Render docs with wdoc"

  p "If you want a static documentation site for your project, drop `page` blocks into a `.wcl` file and let `wcl wdoc` render them. The very page you're reading is built this way."
  code bash {
    source = <<'BASH'
wcl wdoc serve docs/main.wcl              # live preview at http://127.0.0.1:8080
wcl wdoc build docs/main.wcl --out _site  # one-shot static build
BASH
  }

  p "Next: skim the [features tour](features), then keep the [WCL language reference](reference:index) handy while you author."
}
